<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#textLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The language or languages of the text content. Express as a BCP 47 language tag where a standard code exists (e.g., 'ar' for Arabic, 'gez' for Ge'ez). For languages without standard BCP 47 codes, use a descriptive string: 'Old Nubian', 'Coptic', 'Middle Nubian'. Multiple values permitted for polyglot texts or texts in more than one language. Do not conflate language and script — record both separately."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-wood> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#PhysicalSupportScheme> .
