<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-place> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A place, site, crossroads, or territory serves as the medium."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#carriersText> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "carries text"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-divination> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ManifestationMode> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#MediumTypeScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-ostracon> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A pottery sherd or stone flake used as an informal writing surface for short texts, school exercises, receipts, or personal notes. Common in Nubian and Egyptian archaeological contexts; many DBMNT texts are ostraca."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-divination> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Manifestation asserted to occur through divination, oracle, or the interpretive reading of divinatory instruments."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#textLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "text language"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material object serves as the medium — a consecrated vessel, nganga, otán, or ritual artifact."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-auditory> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ManifestationModeScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-clay> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Fired or unfired clay tablets bearing inscribed or impressed text."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#hasMediumType> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-auditory> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#textLanguage> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-person> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A human person serves as the medium, as in possession or mounted manifestation."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#TextContent> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#minimumAccessLevel> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#access-public-unrestricted> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-papyrus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Papyrus"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#hasMediumType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#MediumType> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-possession> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Manifestation asserted to occur through mounting or possession of a medium person. The agent speaks and acts through the medium during the event."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-possession> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Distinguish from embodied: possession involves a medium person who is temporarily occupied; embodied involves a distinct physical presence."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#PhysicalSupportScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-stone> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-instrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Instrument"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#carriedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#support-ostracon> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#textScript> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-possession> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#Medium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medium through which manifestation is asserted to occur — a person, object, place, text, or instrument. A Medium is the vehicle, not the agent; the sacred agent is modeled in iroko-nkisi or iroko-agency. One ManifestationEvent may involve multiple media."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#carriedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "carried by"@en .
