<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ManuscriptObject> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A physical manuscript or archival object — codex, scroll, single leaf, inscribed stone, ostracon, stela, or similar carrier. Models the physical vehicle as distinct from the intellectual content it carries. Structurally equivalent to the Object level in the vHMML three-tier hierarchy (Object / Part / Contents). A ManuscriptObject may carry one or more iroko:TextContent instances. The physical and intellectual levels are modeled separately so that a single text can be located across multiple physical carriers, and a single object can carry multiple texts. Subclass of iroko:DocumentaryEvidence, which is itself a subclass of iroko:SacredEntity."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#MediumTypeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-person> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/isPartOf> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-framework/> .
